# ServiceMatcher Agent — ReAct Migration + Prompt Overhaul

## Decision: Option B — Full ReAct Migration

Based on user feedback: proceed with ReAct migration + prompt overhaul. No live Google Places API — keep seeded DB only.

---

## Current Architecture (Linear Pipeline)

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[intent_parser] --> B{complete?}
    B -->|no| C[clarifier] --> A
    B -->|yes| D[provider_caller] --> E[tool_executor] --> F[ranking] --> G[decision] --> H[booking_step] --> I[followup_step]
```

## New Architecture (ReAct + Response Formatter)

```mermaid
graph TD
    START --> intent_parser
    intent_parser -->|incomplete| clarifier
    clarifier -->|interrupt/resume| intent_parser
    intent_parser -->|complete| react_agent
    react_agent -->|tool_call| tool_executor
    tool_executor --> react_agent
    react_agent -->|final answer| response_formatter
    response_formatter --> booking_step
    booking_step --> followup_step
    followup_step --> END
```

**Key difference:** The middle section (provider discovery → ranking → decision) becomes a ReAct loop where the LLM dynamically decides which tools to call and when to stop. This produces genuine agentic reasoning in the trace.

---

## Risk Mitigation

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|
| Checkpoint schema break | Clear `langgraph_checkpoints` table before deploy |
| ReAct loop gets stuck | `max_iterations=4` hard cap + timeout |
| Higher latency (2-4 LLM calls) | Acceptable for demo; use `gemini-2.0-flash` (fast) |
| Debugging under pressure | Full trace logging preserved in every node |

